Using the ideal gas law at roughly room temperature and 1 atm:

\[
n=\frac{P}{kT}\approx \frac{1.0\times 10^5}{(1.38\times 10^{-23})(300)}
\approx 2.4\times 10^{25}\ \text{m}^{-3}
\]

Convert to cm\(^{-3}\):

\[
2.4\times 10^{25}\ \text{m}^{-3} = 2.4\times 10^{19}\ \text{cm}^{-3}
\]

So there are about \(2.5\times 10^{19}\) molecules per cm\(^3\).

The average spacing is roughly the cube root of the volume per molecule:

\[
d \sim \left(\frac{1}{n}\right)^{1/3}
\approx \left(4\times 10^{-20}\ \text{cm}^3\right)^{1/3}
\approx 3.4\times 10^{-7}\ \text{cm}
\]

This matches option F.

The answer is (F)
